{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1344426-talents-in-game","id":1344426,"title":"Talents in game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-29T08:55:18-07:00","id":1344426,"title":"Talents in game","content":"Hello everybody,<br /> <br /> I am watching Watchmen in HBO, so I had to watch Watchmen movie again, and a nice \u201cfight the organised crime\u201d campaign on the best Watchmen stile.<br /> <br /> Anyone had an campaign Only with Talents? How powerful they are from CharGen? Any tips?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T11:36:41-07:00","id":1344456,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Talents require a little more effort from players to set up their powers to work since most of them don't just always apply by default like a lot of nova powers. But they have some really awesome ones that can wreck opposition even faster than novas or psions can in the right circumstances. In one of my games, for instance, a talent PC managed to get herself invited to the evil bad guy corporation's top board meeting using one of her social powers, something that novas or psions would have had to jump through hoops to accomplsih.<br /> <br /> In direct combat, they're not much more powerful than normal baselines with the same stats, but they're strong enough to beat up organized crime. If you want a more Watchmen style feel, I'd suggest giving them some extra starting XP to purchase attributes and skills to get their dice pools up a little. Their powers are nice but they really need to work on their dice pools too, and there can be a bit of temptation to focus on getting more wacky cool powers than core competence, so giving them early XP that only can be spent on the basics can help offset that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T12:21:47-07:00","id":1344470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1344426-talents-in-game?p=1344456#post1344456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a more Watchmen style feel, I'd suggest giving them some extra starting XP to purchase attributes and skills to get their dice pools up a little. Their powers are nice but they really need to work on their dice pools too, and there can be a bit of temptation to focus on getting more wacky cool powers than core competence, so giving them early XP that only can be spent on the basics can help offset that.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to keep them from spending it on facets, inspiration, and gifts, consider giving them some Path dots. That'll give them skill and edge points to spend without being able to increase their wacky, cool powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T13:37:08-07:00","id":1344490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1344426-talents-in-game?p=1344470#post1344470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to keep them from spending it on facets, inspiration, and gifts, consider giving them some Path dots. That'll give them skill and edge points to spend without being able to increase their wacky, cool powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, that's a great idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T15:27:09-07:00","id":1344513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1344426-talents-in-game?p=1344470#post1344470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to keep them from spending it on facets, inspiration, and gifts, consider giving them some Path dots. That'll give them skill and edge points to spend without being able to increase their wacky, cool powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was just about to make that same suggestion. I'm actually considering bumping Paths up to 4 at chargen as a blanket rule. Either bump an existing path up to 2, or add a fourth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T17:31:40-07:00","id":1344535,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of more path dots from start, it gives some depth to character, more about what he knows, what he is god at and who he deals with, in the opposite to the more flashy stuff like powers.<br /> <br /> i used to play a Adventure! campaign with only Daredevils and it was fun, more about how to do stuff and less about charging enemies, but still, Daredevils with the proper knacks used to be pretty good at fighting mobs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T07:32:03-07:00","id":1344653,"title":"","content":"Having some &quot;stock&quot; superhero gear beforehand might help. Inspired teck that impart Knacks that promote two-fisted action in particular. For example:<br /> <br /> <b>Cowl </b>(Calm Blue Ocean, Don't Mess With Me)<br /> <b>Utility Belt</b> (Device Mogul, Knee-Deep in Brass)<br /> <b>Exosuit</b> (Internal Thermostat, The Late Late Shift, Last Ditch Effort, Unrelenting)<br /> <b>Power Gloves</b> (Fists of Stone, Speak Softly)<br /> <br /> There might even be super-science dealers who make and sell Inspired or otherwise advanced technology and the like. A black market of Nazi and Cold-War era super serum, mutagenic compounds and sketchy cybernetics is a great story element.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, Mutation extras would be pretty cool.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 10-30-2019, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:29:30-07:00","id":1345301,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the more I think about it the more I think a Talents only game could be really really really fun. I mean its for somewhat larger then life figures, but not to the point where they use super powers. So say the members of SG-1 or those on Stargate Atlantis or even the non-Jedi of Star Wars (Han's luck is totally something Inspired) and on and on. But even more the fact that there is something a bit more than normal is also really cool, as it allows for &quot;I know what I did is special&quot; and then comes an adventure to prove or expand it. (Maybe one day even letting them take certain Gifts from the other categories)<br /> <br /> My recent mental idea is the whole idea of a Talent being the main character of a Myst game. Being influenced by the energies of the Void they game somewhat enhanced abilities. <br /> <br /> But yeah, I think a Talent only game is perfect! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:37:14-07:00","id":1345308,"title":"","content":"Of course a Talents only game can be fun; the setting in TC Core features exactly that. The only difference between that and what Mateus Luz described in his first post is the addition of costumes and codenames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T14:00:54-07:00","id":1345322,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, I was just saying its a pretty brilliant fact. Not that I came up with it. hehe<br /> <br /> Anyway, one thing I was thinking about is the potential of changing the Target Number for Talents from 8 to 7 in a Talent Only game. The nature of this means that success is much easier and so tougher things could be thrown at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}